id: pm-web-s99c
title: Expose every public fleet package and run enabled extension commands
description: "List all 22 public fleet identities with canonical npm, manifest, README and native Cargo facts. Distinguish 17 npm-published extensions, four unpublished extensions and the pre-release native Rust CLI. Install and enable published packages per project, expose documented commands with exact argument handling and retain command output. Verify compiled HTTP behavior with real tracker, registry and SSE acceptance plus behavioral revert proofs; preserve SDK 2026.10.10 and strict canonical discovery when merging main."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-05T05:18:01.915Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T09:25:04.736Z"
author: codex-sol
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Current package catalog and committed fleet snapshot include verified pm-jev metadata and all optional live-fleet completeness assertions pass.
actual_result: "PR182 renewed directory-order nit5477988575 fixed with locale-independent lexicographic sort before existing discovery; same2 real assignments assert exact first-folder full metadata and second-folder conflict. Host old-source baseline3/3 passes, so cross-platform contract correction without fabricated revert failure. New full linked release492/492 zero skips; configured34 src S/L90.33 B80.10 F93.43; packed npm/nativeBun4/4 hosts10.4/10.9, standaloneSDK10.9. Source/distribution rebuilt and fingerprint stable. Strict owner history verified; local pinned health blocked by managed extension10.10 versusSDK10.9. Owners/reviews/whole-source/privacy/dev4high/graph/concurrency/hosted gates open, SDK4 hosting unchanged; no closure/deployment."
comments[49]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T20:23:20.330Z",codex-sol,"Baseline acceptance against the built package and a real scratch tracker: findCatalogEntry('pm-jev') is undefined. The canonical live-fleet catalog suite passes 8/12 and fails four assertions, including missing pm-jev membership and stale snapshot. Verified current manifest capabilities commands/schema, local-first Ollama default and optional hosted privacy opt-in. Registry lookup npm view pm-jev version returns E404, so availability must be unreleased despite publishConfig intent. Plan: refresh verified metadata and links, regenerate the registry-backed snapshot, retain every completeness assertion."
  "2026-10-07T21:52:30.765Z",codex-sol,"Implementation includes manifest-exact metadata, verified docs/npm/repository/report links, visible local-provider and optional hosted credential requirements, and unreleased availability based on E404. The online generator refreshed the complete 21-extension snapshot. Canonical live-fleet catalog checks now pass 12/12. Behavioral revert removing only the Jev catalog entry from the built implementation fails acceptance with an AssertionError for missing pm-jev; restored behavior passes."
  "2026-10-07T22:09:11.976Z",codex-sol,"The final npm coverage phase passes all 484 tests against the complete canonical fleet, with 33 src files reported: statements/lines 90.25%, branches 79.57%, functions 93.90%. Configured thresholds remain 90/90/79/92, and discovery/catalog services are 100% in all four dimensions. The production audit is clean. Packed acceptance and final policy checks are still running; this is a scoped src coverage receipt, not a whole-repository or hosted readiness claim."
  "2026-10-07T22:16:57.480Z",codex-sol,"Close-ready: both complete npm run release:check and bun run release:check pass against the complete canonical fleet with isolated external scratch fixtures. Each passes 484/484 tests and packed npm/Bun consumers on pm host 2026.10.4; audit reports zero production vulnerabilities. Configured src inventory is 33 files: npm statements/lines 90.25%, branches 79.57%, functions 93.90%; Bun 90.27%, 79.63%, 93.90%. Thresholds stay 90/90/79/92, duplication is zero, and all type/lint/docstring/changelog/workflow gates pass. Final registry lookup still returns E404 for pm-jev. Linked pm acceptance passes 13/13. Metadata, links, snapshot, README and acceptance documentation are complete; no hosted deployment validation is claimed."
  "2026-10-10T03:00:48.106Z",codex-sol,"SDK update candidate full unchanged release run still fails four catalog checks: membership, resolvable fleet manifests, missing pm-jev, and snapshot fidelity. Independent PR #175 source/discovery/built-catalog tests pass 16/16, and npm still returns 404 for pm-jev. GitHub reports #175 conflicting at d883781d6d134694bedddd65ad37011aa2cbcdea; CodeRabbit reports no actionable findings while other requested reviews are unavailable. Do not conflate this bounded isolated check with live fleet freshness or merge approval."
  "2026-10-10T03:15:11.510Z",codex-sol,"PR175 at d883781d6d134694bedddd65ad37011aa2cbcdea already implements pm-jev metadata, registry availability, UI links and built real-SDK acceptance. Reuse those relevant hunks on PR182; no independent catalog design or imported tracker owners. Regenerate the snapshot from current canonical metadata and registry instead of copying a dated receipt."
  "2026-10-10T04:07:49.305Z",codex-sol,"Verification receipt is recorded in docs/sdk-update-automation.md and linked from pm-web-8pml: complete release490/490,zero skips; packed npm/nativeBun4/4, six real disposablePostgreSQL collaboration tests. Keep item unclosed for independent orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-10T04:47:33.719Z",codex-sol,"Continue existing PR #182 at clean base 4ff3ec41fff7ea4e25d3155978f1bdf4bdc7ca9e. Verify CodeRabbit inline 4236357377 against real catalog, UI contracts and registry snapshot; repair only unsupported npm links, preserve published links, add real catalog/UI regression and source revert proof. Feature owner pm-web-8pml and whole-source quality owner pm-web-fy9a remain open; companion owner pm-cli-website-session-2026-10-10 owns crosslinks. No dependency, threshold, deadline, telemetry or hosted change."
  "2026-10-10T04:49:24.888Z",codex-sol,"Finding confirmed: live registry GET pm-jev returns 404; committed snapshot npmPublished:false and availability:unreleased. Both link contracts required npm and the renderer enumerated Jev's explicit URL. New real catalog/UI regression fails baseline (1/2), while published Graph links from the installed package metadata pass. Make only npm optional, omit Jev URL, retain docs/repository/report, and preserve published links and four packed npm/native-Bun scenarios. Quota refreshed: codex forecast 44 percent, 70 percent remaining; no subagent launch needed."
  "2026-10-10T04:51:51.208Z",codex-sol,"Source revert proof restores only package-catalog.ts from base 4ff3ec; the new real UI regression fails on the rendered Jev npm anchor (1/2), while published Graph control still passes. Restoring candidate bytes yields 15/15 focused catalog/built/UI tests, zero skips. Build, lint, server/browser and test typechecks pass. Extend the existing four packed scenarios with imports of the installed tarball catalog/browser renderer under each actual Node/native-Bun runtime; retain all original SDK/host/status checks."
  "2026-10-10T04:53:08.024Z",codex-sol,"The linked coverage invocation exhausted pm test's default 120-second runner budget and returned a timeout; this is missing coverage evidence, not an assertion pass. Run the same npm run coverage command directly against the own disposable PostgreSQL fixture. Application deadlines, coverage thresholds and source inventory remain unchanged. Packed acceptance is independently running with all four original scenarios and the new installed-catalog/UI contract checks."
  "2026-10-10T04:55:43.119Z",codex-sol,"Final source/test/package/distribution fingerprint is fb5c50fef054e353db7e15434dc715226c60658e8defa71b4dd1597cd371648f over 285 sorted repository-relative paths (path NUL bytes NUL, SHA-256). Build and both source/test typechecks pass; lint passes; duplication remains 0 percent over 45021 lines and 156 sources; docstring gate passes 95 files and 625 declarations. PM health ok with 13 stale-item advisories; validation ok with existing metadata/file-link/linked-trust warnings. Full coverage and four-scenario installed tarball checks remain pending; do not infer release readiness."
  "2026-10-10T05:05:31.803Z",codex-sol,"First complete direct coverage run exits 1: 491/492 tests pass, zero skips; sole failure is unchanged 2000-item graph bound at 15811 ms (pm-web-hqqp). All catalog/UI, built package, snapshot, route and six real collaboration tests pass. Focused existing large-corpus check subsequently passes 1/1 at 4495 ms after all four packed scenarios pass. Canonical coverage reports are correctly invalidated. Repeat only unchanged coverage now, without packed installation overlap; no source, deadline, threshold or exclusion changes."
  "2026-10-10T05:13:10.938Z",codex-sol,"Final unchanged coverage retry exits 0: 492/492 tests, zero skips, all 34 configured server files present. Accepted c8 S/L 90.32 percent (10321/11426, 1105 remaining each), B 80.18 (1768/2205, 437 remaining), F 93.43 (256/274, 18 remaining). Browser/tooling source remains outside the denominator; no all-source 100-percent claim. Instrumented 2000-item graph read 3257 ms; all six genuine collaboration tests pass. Retain earlier linked timeout and complete 491/492 timing-failure receipts, focused 4495 ms success, all four packed passes and real source-revert failure. Source fingerprint fb5c50fef054e353db7e15434dc715226c60658e8defa71b4dd1597cd371648f remains unchanged. Receipts are in docs/sdk-update-automation.md. Required exact-head reviews, whole-source quality, development audit, historical privacy and hosted readiness stay open. Release claim without closing; no bots, merge, publication or deployment."
  "2026-10-10T05:35:32.684Z",codex-sol,"CodeRabbit4236540807 verified on real filesystem. With two directory/name assignments, the prior assertion fails because the conflict record can be retained. Corrected assertion accepts exactly either full metadata record and still requires a conflict diagnostic. Complete existing discovery file3/3, zero skips; test typechecking and lint pass. No scanner, production, distribution, dependencies, timing bounds, coverage thresholds or exclusions changed. Earlier492/492 and4 packed gates are receipts for af430dd; renewed exact-head CI/review remains required. docs/sdk-update-automation.md records this correction."
  "2026-10-10T06:59:26.253Z",codex-sol,"Renewed PR182 review 5477988575 verified on 97de322: directory enumeration controls the retained conflicting worktree record. Sort actual string-named Dirent entries lexicographically before the existing loop; preserve complete metadata and explicit conflict refusal. Tighten the existing two real folder assignments without mocked filesystem counts or duplicate tests. Check real host ordering honestly before asserting old-behavior failure; rerun full current-source and four packed host/runtime gates under pm-web-8pml."
  "2026-10-10T06:59:58.863Z",codex-sol,"The tightened real-layout baseline passes 3/3 on this host: actual directory enumeration already selects first lexicographically in both assignments. This is an explicit cross-platform contract correction, not fabricated fail-on-revert proof. Installed Node types define Dirent<Name extends string | Buffer = string>; the withFileTypes:true default encoding overload returns Dirent<string>[]. Sort string names using code-unit comparisons without locale dependence; preserve every candidate field and require the exact second-folder conflict plus all malformed diagnostics."
  "2026-10-10T07:12:43.213Z",codex-sol,"Renewed review5477988575 repaired: locale-independent lexicographic entry sort before the existing discovery loop, complete retained metadata and conflict refusal unchanged. Existing two real folder assignments now select exact first-folder metadata and require exact second-folder conflict plus all malformed diagnostics. Tightened baseline3/3 already passes on this host: honest cross-platform contract correction, no fail-on-revert claim. New full linked release gate passes492/492 zero skips; configured34-source S/L90.33 B80.10 F93.43; all4 packed npm/nativeBun minimum/current hosts pass. Source fingerprint6f02e7d92d3b78c1e68e284f3b78d7983ed4c45889693573e3fa26102f6ec7a8 unchanged. docs/sdk-update-automation.md records commands and receipts. Keep owner open; historical af430dd receipts superseded only for this candidate, independent gates remain."
  "2026-10-11T05:12:17.466Z",codex-sol,"Merged main while preserving the SDK 2026.10.10 upgrade, deterministic discovery and unpublished-link guard. Extended the public catalog to all 22 fleet identities with source-backed npm names, descriptions, capabilities, commands and links. Rust is a separate pre-release native CLI with no npm identity or extension capabilities. Added project-scoped documented command execution and built HTTP acceptance with a real tracker and registry Presets installation."
  "2026-10-11T05:13:27.281Z",codex-sol,"Real npm Presets installation and activation passed. Command execution exposed a pm-web adapter defect: extension nested positionals are dropped and boolean arity comes only from core tool parameters. The command endpoint now selects the bounded process path using the existing timeout option, preserving exact extension arguments without a shell. This addresses the consumer adapter; no upstream SDK defect was established."
  "2026-10-11T05:17:52.362Z",codex-sol,"Built HTTP acceptance now passes 1/1 with a real initialized tracker, registry-installed Presets, installed/enabled/runtime-active state and the documented nested presets list command. It lists all 22 public identities, refuses unpublished ADO and native Rust with distinct 409 explanations, denies view-only command execution and rejects malformed arguments or workspace selectors. Catalog/card/worktree checks pass 20/20. Behavioral native-entry revert already fails its exact catalog assertion; command-path revert is running."
  "2026-10-11T05:19:48.875Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof completed on the built server: removing only the native Rust catalog entry fails the exact 22-identity assertion; removing only the extension command route timeout/process selection fails the documented Presets command assertion (400 instead of 200). Each experiment executes one test with one AssertionError, zero module-load or syntax failures. Original source bytes were restored and the server rebuilt after each experiment."
  "2026-10-11T05:23:32.484Z",codex-sol,"The linked acceptance command uses schema PM context with the package source workspace; its fixture always initializes its own real tracker and pins the fixture PM_PATH. The no-context/source combination is correctly refused by the linked runner, so the persisted entry now uses the supported default context rather than relying on an override."
  "2026-10-11T05:25:08.041Z",codex-sol,"PM-linked built install/run acceptance passes 1/1 with zero skips after restoring both behavioral reverts. Existing canonical catalog/card/worktree focused checks pass 20/20. The npm release gate runs under an empty HOME, disabled global/system Git configuration, the complete canonical fleet and an external CommonJS/Git temporary root. Coverage and duplication thresholds and all configured source/test lists are unchanged."
  "2026-10-11T05:27:45.319Z",codex-sol,The first npm gate exposed two historical route assertions that assumed every catalog row was an npm extension or template. Updated them to require the native category and its specific refusal reason while retaining the no-spawn check for every unreleased package. The release gate will be rerun with unchanged thresholds; the original failure remains recorded.
  "2026-10-11T05:30:16.069Z",codex-sol,"Corrected route regressions pass 9/9 with zero failures or skips under isolated Git identity. Stopped the first full npm attempt after its two now-corrected historical assertions failed, reducing concurrent heavy validation while preserving the failed output. Source thresholds and graph timing limits remain unchanged. Built install/enable/command acceptance and both behavioral revert proofs remain passing."
  "2026-10-11T05:35:25.649Z",codex-sol,"CI now executes the literal npm run release:check and bun run release:check commands under a fresh HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration on both existing Node matrix lines. The npm step includes the previous coverage command plus every release check; existing dist, health, audit, packed acceptance and changelog checks remain. This gives independent exact-head gate evidence while preserving all original source/test inventories, assertions and thresholds. Shared-host failed timing evidence remains recorded."
  "2026-10-11T05:44:09.326Z",codex-sol,"Final UI review found command execution announced a package-state event, which could redraw the originating card before its output appeared. Removed that event from the command route. Extended built HTTP acceptance to observe the real SSE connection: install, activation and deactivation events remain, command execution emits no package-state refresh. Restored acceptance passes 1/1 with zero skips. Current independent CI npm release gates passed on Node 22 and 26; Bun is running. A final head will include the feedback correction and refreshed behavioral revert proofs."
  "2026-10-11T05:49:15.430Z",codex-sol,"All three behavioral revert experiments were refreshed against the extended built HTTP/SSE acceptance. Removing only native Rust fails the exact 22-identity assertion; removing only explicit process selection fails Presets execution (400 versus 200); restoring only the former command package-state broadcast fails the real SSE feedback assertion. Each executes one test with one behavioral AssertionError, no syntax/module-load failures. Original source bytes were restored and the compiled server rebuilt after each experiment."
  "2026-10-11T05:51:14.676Z",codex-sol,Final PM-linked real HTTP/SSE acceptance passes 1/1 with zero failures/skips after all three source variants were restored and rebuilt. Current strict local PM health reports a managed GitHub extension host/SDK skew (2026.10.10 versus 2026.10.11); tracked integrity/history checks remain clean. Independent CI installs the pinned managed extension in a fresh checkout and passed strict health and both full release commands on Node 22/26. Preserve the local health boundary; do not alter global extension state or claim that local health is green.
  "2026-10-11T06:05:06.742Z",codex-sol,"Final catalog implementation head f4f7dc1 is verified by independent CI run 38116214351. Literal npm run release:check and bun run release:check pass on both Node 22 and 26, each 496/496 tests, zero failures/skips. This includes the extended real HTTP/SSE registry install, activation and command acceptance plus all main regressions. All 34 configured server sources meet unchanged thresholds, all four packed current/minimum npm/Bun scenarios pass, and fresh-checkout strict PM health and committed dist checks pass. Record-only follow-up preserves identical runtime, tests, dependencies, dist and workflow inputs; local failed/stopped attempts and managed-extension skew remain documented."
  "2026-10-11T06:36:48.557Z",codex-sol,"Verified all four round-1 findings on PR #175. Plan: empty command arguments with the help placeholder retained; preserve structured failed-command output; reject legacy --path selectors before runner dispatch; bound the deactivation SSE wait so cleanup executes. Add behavioral regression and revert evidence, then rebuild and run unchanged npm and Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-11T06:42:16.909Z",codex-sol,Implemented the four round-1 fixes. UI regression passes 6/6 after correcting its compiled-state import. Empty-argument and failed-output behavioral reverts each execute one test and fail with one AssertionError; the original sources are restored and rebuilt between experiments. The initial combined acceptance passed the real HTTP/SSE install/run test and deadline test; its new UI test fixture needed the compiled singleton correction. Pinned CLI help confirms --pm-path is preferred over legacy --path.
  "2026-10-11T06:42:30.486Z",codex-sol,"All four behavioral revert proofs completed: restoring the help default fails the enabled-card assertion; restoring output-discarding catch fails stdout feedback; removing only --path from the selector set fails the real HTTP assertion (409 versus 400); removing only the SSE deadline fails the watchdog assertion (unbounded versus rejected). Each run executes one test with one AssertionError and no module-load failure. Restored every source and rebuilt affected output. Both legacy selector forms are covered by the acceptance, and the missing-event regression verifies finally cleanup."
  "2026-10-11T07:02:01.386Z",codex-sol,"Restored PM-linked acceptance passes 8/8 with zero failures or skips; linked-result recording is disabled by project policy, so this comment records the receipt. Full isolated-identity npm coverage hit the existing pm-web-hqqp graph latency boundary: the 2000-item certified read took 23045 ms. Leave the limit and graph implementation unchanged; both requested full runs continue, with the local failure preserved."
  "2026-10-11T07:11:45.094Z",codex-sol,Canonical fleet validation passes 12/12 with zero skips when PM_FLEET_ROOT explicitly selects the canonical package inventory. The initial complete npm run defaulted to the sibling worktree farm and therefore reports two expected metadata-consistency failures in addition to the existing graph latency failure. Preserve the unsuccessful run and select the canonical inventory for subsequent validation; do not refresh the verified snapshot from worktree candidates.
  "2026-10-11T07:17:52.040Z",codex-sol,"Initial isolated-identity npm release run completes 498 tests: 494 pass, 4 fail, zero skips/cancellations. Failures are two catalog assertions from the implicit sibling-worktree fleet root, the existing 23045 ms versus 10000 ms graph read budget, and the unchanged server-entrypoint test timing out at its 10000 ms subprocess deadline. All new correction regressions and built install/run/SSE acceptance pass. Replaced the automatic Bun preflight before coverage with a complete Bun run selecting the canonical fleet root. The earlier Bun preflight is interrupted evidence, not a passing gate."
  "2026-10-11T07:20:41.667Z",codex-sol,Created follow-up pm-web-qdhx after searching existing startup/entrypoint work. It records the full-coverage missing-database subprocess deadline failure without asserting an SDK defect or changing the guard/deadline. Graph timing evidence remains on existing pm-web-hqqp. All follow-ups remain open.
  "2026-10-11T07:39:27.936Z",codex-sol,"Both requested full release commands completed their coverage suites with unchanged source inventories and thresholds. Initial npm: 494/498, four failures (two implicit worktree-farm catalog assertions plus graph/startup budgets), zero skips. Corrected canonical-root Bun: 496/498, two failures (12565 ms graph read versus 10000 ms and independent-process fixture overlap), zero skips. New correction regressions and built acceptance pass in both. Production audit independently passes with zero vulnerabilities. Remaining packaging and release-policy checks are being executed directly; these results cannot make either unsuccessful full command a passing gate."
  "2026-10-11T07:46:21.413Z",codex-sol,"Round-1 work is ready for review: command args default to [] with the help placeholder retained; ApiError preserves failed-command JSON so stdout and stderr remain visible; legacy --path and --path=value selectors are rejected before extension-state reads and runner dispatch; a 5000 ms deactivation deadline rejects missing SSE and clears its timer so acceptance cleanup runs. Regression acceptance passes 8/8; canonical catalog passes 12/12; each of four behavior-only reverts executes one test and produces one AssertionError, with restored sources rebuilt afterward. Both complete release commands retain failed results: npm 494/498 (initial fleet-root setup plus graph/startup failures), canonical-root Bun 496/498 (graph and process-overlap failures), zero skips. Follow-ups pm-web-hqqp and pm-web-qdhx preserve timing evidence; focused startup and process tests each pass 1/1. Independent remaining checks pass: production audit zero vulnerabilities, packed current/minimum npm/native-Bun consumers 4/4, pack dry-run, changelog date and publish attestation. Types, lint, zero duplication and docstrings pass. No thresholds or inventories changed; no passing full-gate receipt is claimed. Linked-test persistence is disabled, so results are recorded in comments. Leave every item open."
  "2026-10-11T08:51:33.956Z",codex-agent,"Round 2: verifying the pinned CLI effective command ownership contract before dispatch. Plan: refuse catalog command owner collisions, prove with a real scratch project and local duplicate handler, run an isolated behavioural revert, rebuild, and run both release gates."
  "2026-10-11T08:54:54.169Z",codex-agent,"Verified CLI 2026.10.10 ownership contract: published docs/EXTENSIONS.md lines 289/355 and exported dist/sdk/extension/describe.d.ts define command_ownership, ordered claimants, winner, and last_activated_wins. Runner probes the entire table in its workspace queue using the execution binary/environment, requires exact-path handler/override winners to equal the catalog name, and refuses unavailable ownership. Built real-HTTP acceptance passes 2/2: npm Presets, later-priority local duplicate, verified direct CLI dispatch to the duplicate, HTTP 409 naming scratch-shadow with no execution marker/settings mutation, and normal execution after disabling the duplicate. External filesystem changes remain outside the web queue."
  "2026-10-11T08:55:49.578Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: restored only runPm to its pre-fix implementation, retained the real collision regression and route changes, rebuilt server output, and ran node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern='built server executes npm Presets' test/catalog-install-e2e.test.ts. Result 0/1, one AssertionError: expected HTTP 409, got HTTP 200 with output owner scratch-shadow. Original fixed source bytes restored and server rebuilt successfully. This proves actual wrong-package execution, not a load/syntax failure."
  "2026-10-11T08:56:31.800Z",codex-agent,"PM-linked test index 7 completed successfully (one linked command, built HTTP acceptance 2/2). Existing project policy reports evidence_recording.recorded=false, reason tracking_disabled; results are retained in these comments without changing policy. Beginning unchanged-threshold npm and Bun release checks with isolated Git identity, an external CommonJS scratch root, and canonical fleet metadata."
  "2026-10-11T09:04:04.624Z",codex-agent,"Initial full npm release check: all 498/498 tests passed, zero skips/cancellations, but statements/lines 89.89% failed unchanged 90% thresholds (branches 80.09%, functions 93.09%). Built-only acceptance was outside the source coverage counters. The same real HTTP scenario now runs against both built and source apps. Probe and dispatch also share the project-key environment; the duplicate fixture only registers when that key is present, so it verifies runtime-environment parity. Rebuilding, rerunning the focused acceptance and revert proof, then running both full gates on the final implementation."
  "2026-10-11T09:05:05.932Z",codex-agent,"Final source/built acceptance passes 3/3 (zero skips/cancellations). Repeated behavioural revert on the environment-sensitive fixture: restore only pre-fix runPm, rebuild server, run node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern='built server executes npm Presets' test/catalog-install-e2e.test.ts => 0/1, one AssertionError, HTTP 200 instead of 409 with owner scratch-shadow. Fixed source bytes restored exactly and server rebuilt. Running the final linked acceptance and both unchanged-threshold release gates."
  "2026-10-11T09:05:58.610Z",codex-agent,Final PM-linked test index 7 passes (one linked command; built/source HTTP acceptance 3/3). Result persistence remains tracking_disabled by existing project policy; comment receipts preserve the evidence.
  "2026-10-11T09:15:57.761Z",codex-agent,"Final isolated-identity npm run release:check PASSED: 499/499 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations; 34 configured source files; statements/lines 90.51%, branches 80.50%, functions 93.45%, unchanged thresholds. Type checks, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, production audit (0 vulnerabilities), pack dry-run, four packed npm/native-Bun current/minimum-host scenarios (2026.10.10/2026.10.4), changelog check, release-date and attestation checks all pass. Source/test hashes unchanged. Starting the final Bun release check."
  "2026-10-11T09:25:03.669Z",codex-agent,"Final isolated-identity bun run release:check PASSED: 499/499 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations; 34 configured source files; statements/lines 90.51%, branches 80.50%, functions 93.45% at unchanged thresholds. All type/lint/zero-duplication/docstring/audit/pack/changelog/release-policy checks pass, including four packed npm/native-Bun current/minimum-host scenarios. Both complete gates now pass on unchanged source/test hashes. Final focused and linked acceptance pass 3/3; the function-only rebuilt revert fails 0/1 with HTTP 200 and scratch-shadow output instead of 409. Supported command_ownership contract exists in CLI 2026.10.10; no new CLI/SDK ownership gap. Existing linked-result tracking policy is disabled. External package/code changes are outside the web queue. Ready to commit the source, rebuilt output, docs and tracker, push PR 175, and reply to thread 4240940241 without resolving it. Item remains in progress; releasing the claim."
